01:47.520 --> 01:47.720
Yeah.

01:47.820 --> 01:56.140
So, I mean, like I said, the second series, the second and third examples were less interesting to me.

01:56.140 --> 02:07.560
But, you know, they are images of orbs transiting from coastal facilities out to the ocean and sort of describing...

02:07.600 --> 02:17.110
You know, what those facilities were as, I think, the unspoken implication of why something like this would be out there.

02:19.830 --> 02:32.250
And, yes, just a similar or just a bit not vague, but a general description of we observed this coming from this direction or from where this facility, sensitive facility was left over the ocean.

02:33.630 --> 02:37.370
You know, this was our task asset and it happened on this date.

02:37.370 --> 02:38.270
Anything...

02:38.690 --> 02:43.190
Really striking in the rest of that document that really highlighted to you.

02:43.470 --> 02:45.310
Anything else in that document that was really striking?

02:45.810 --> 02:46.050
Yeah.

02:46.190 --> 02:51.830
So the last example of the four was back to Russia again.

02:51.830 --> 02:54.230
This time, I believe, in the Atlantic Ocean.

02:55.070 --> 03:00.550
And it shows another Russian intelligence vessel underway this time at night.

03:01.130 --> 03:03.290
