03:05.670 --> 03:08.830
And it shows above this Russian.

03:08.850 --> 03:21.630
Vessel is another black triangle, but where is the first example in the Pacific was an equilateral, large, pretty stunning object that was of comparable size to the vessels below it.

03:21.630 --> 03:31.230
This was a more definitely smaller, is smaller than the vessel, and it was more angular in shape and sort of swept back.

03:31.770 --> 03:38.770
And it was also accompanied by text saying that there was no indication that the Russian vessel was responding in any way to this.

03:39.530 --> 03:40.730
Ship hovering above it.

03:41.690 --> 03:46.650
And it did not describe in this instance whether it had miraculously appeared or if it was tailing the ship.

03:46.870 --> 03:48.990
But triangular in shape and hovering.

03:50.050 --> 03:52.630
Well, hovering probably matching speed, though, too, with the ship.

03:53.270 --> 03:58.450
Like USS Russell, other people argue, and I don't care what shape it is.

03:58.830 --> 04:03.790
You know, when you have something with range finders off of a ship that goes with it, stops with the ship, continues.

04:04.010 --> 04:08.870
So this is not a new thing, this idea of triangular by angle of observation pyramid.

04:08.930 --> 04:09.690
It's not a new thing, this idea of triangular by angle of observation pyramid.

04:09.690 --> 04:10.370
Some would say.

04:10.570 --> 04:10.650
Could be.

04:11.050 --> 04:11.370
Right.

04:11.610 --> 04:12.610
So that's striking.

04:12.890 --> 04:13.910
And you saw that, too.

04:14.150 --> 04:14.430
Yes.

04:14.870 --> 04:15.030
Yeah.

04:15.030 --> 04:16.130
And that was the last example.

04:16.850 --> 04:27.430
After that was sort of a summary slide or two about just recapping, like, the fact that these incidents are, we are collecting, sorry, we are collecting these incidents around the world.

04:28.270 --> 04:38.550
That we are focused on UAPRB collection incidents by tasked and untasked assets and the collection and analysis of those data.

04:39.690 --> 04:42.150
So sometimes we know where it's going to be, tasked assets.

04:42.350 --> 04:45.230
Sometimes we just happen to capture them, untasked assets.

04:45.250 --> 04:45.530
Correct.

04:45.810 --> 04:46.170
Correct.

04:46.330 --> 04:52.230
And I think a good example is in that brief itself, where the orb incidents appeared to be untasked assets.

04:52.370 --> 04:54.190
They were not there to collect on orbs.

04:54.210 --> 04:55.850
They were there to collect on something else.

04:55.850 --> 04:57.110
And they happened to catch something.

04:58.230 --> 05:00.850
