05:02.180 --> 05:05.560
We were there to watch the Russians and their Russians' interactions with this technology.

05:06.220 --> 05:06.260
Wow.

05:06.580 --> 05:09.000
So your suspicions after seeing this 12-page.

05:09.120 --> 05:13.120
Report is that these are freeze frames of what are.

05:13.220 --> 05:13.640
Videos.

05:13.880 --> 05:14.020
Yeah.

05:14.240 --> 05:14.720
Videos.

05:14.940 --> 05:18.520
So somewhere there's a bigger collection of this stuff that's also very interesting.

05:19.060 --> 05:19.400
Absolutely.

05:19.580 --> 05:19.760
Yeah.

05:20.760 --> 05:30.090
Like, you know, there was informal collections of this stuff by interested people on those systems.

05:30.430 --> 05:37.560
And there's absolutely a professional mission-tasked databases for this.

05:37.920 --> 05:38.100
Okay.

05:38.540 --> 05:39.640
So you've seen.

05:39.960 --> 05:40.580
Now you have this.

05:40.660 --> 05:41.100
You've seen a lot of exposure.

05:42.400 --> 05:44.680
You try to do the right thing.

05:45.140 --> 05:47.680
And you take great steps to try to do.

05:48.020 --> 05:49.380
It takes a little while for you.

05:49.420 --> 05:49.860
It does.

05:50.020 --> 05:52.100
So explain that to me, what you tried to do.

05:52.160 --> 05:52.680
So there you go.

05:52.720 --> 05:55.820
You see something that you know shouldn't be there on that archive.

05:56.240 --> 05:57.100
You know, what happens?

05:57.100 --> 05:57.700
What do you do?

05:58.560 --> 05:59.320
Absolutely nothing.

06:00.120 --> 06:03.780
In fact, the first time I read that, I don't know what I just read and if it's even real.

06:04.520 --> 06:06.340
Maybe somebody just made this thing.

06:06.700 --> 06:06.820
Okay.

06:06.860 --> 06:07.460
Explain that.

06:07.580 --> 06:08.080
So you can.

06:08.280 --> 06:09.640
It would be like a joke or something.

06:09.800 --> 06:10.620
Or they put it.

06:10.660 --> 06:12.800
They put it together literally for a war game, right?

06:13.340 --> 06:18.750
They had maybe created an imaginary program that maybe they wanted to have, right?

06:19.290 --> 06:27.070
Or a desired capability or something that was a representative of the true thing to be used.

06:27.750 --> 06:29.230
Is that normal or common now?

06:29.290 --> 06:30.110
That's a weird thought.

06:30.370 --> 06:34.210
It is a weird thought, but this is what's going through my head because it's so bizarre.

06:34.450 --> 06:34.710
Okay.

06:35.150 --> 06:35.590
And.

06:36.250 --> 06:37.510
You're like, no way.

06:37.730 --> 06:37.950
Yeah.

06:38.090 --> 06:39.450
I'm going through everything.

06:40.270 --> 06:41.050
All the options.

06:41.050 --> 06:42.130
Why it's not what it is.

06:42.170 --> 06:42.350
Right.

06:43.480 --> 06:43.760
Yeah.

06:43.960 --> 06:47.020
And so I do nothing for some time.

06:47.020 --> 06:54.360
And then we, uh, our office gets a training on like, or a refresh training, but this was

06:54.360 --> 06:54.940
new in my career.

06:55.020 --> 06:58.700
So my first time on what to do in cases of spillage for sap material.

06:58.900 --> 06:59.140
Okay.

06:59.720 --> 07:03.960
And I realized, well, no matter how weird this is, this has all the hallmarks of what

07:03.960 --> 07:05.920
you guys just said is a big fucking deal.

07:06.640 --> 07:11.800
So, you know, I can either pretend like I didn't open and read this.

07:11.800 --> 07:17.140
This thing 80 times and hope that, uh, it doesn't notice that either, or I can report it myself.

07:17.800 --> 07:19.960
Uh, so I did that, or I tried to do that.

07:20.710 --> 07:21.830
You tried to report it.

07:22.150 --> 07:24.150
You read it a bunch as it's fascinating.

07:24.150 --> 07:25.250
And then you, you try to report it.

07:25.250 --> 07:26.770
So what does that look like when you try to report that?

07:26.770 --> 07:27.210
What'd you do?

07:27.790 --> 07:36.770
So the first time, uh, I, I went, uh, just quietly to, uh, my, I guess my immediate supervisor, a retired, uh, army colonel.

07:37.110 --> 07:39.630
So you go to your, uh, supervisor, superior.

07:39.950 --> 07:40.270
Mm-hmm.

07:40.270 --> 07:40.770
What would.

07:40.950 --> 07:41.810
I gotta say, Hey, I got a.

07:41.830 --> 07:44.110
Show you something in, in our, in our closet.

07:44.770 --> 07:48.010
Uh, our whole office is a skiff, but inside the skiff is another tiny skiff.

07:48.630 --> 07:52.450
Um, and I think we, we have like a, a spillage things.

07:52.570 --> 07:55.070
And so I need to show it to you, cuz this is apparently what we're supposed to do.

07:55.070 --> 07:55.930
Show it to your boss.

07:56.170 --> 08:02.050
Um, and then follow the reporting chain and you sign, you sign a paper and that's how it's supposed to be handled all by the books.

08:02.050 --> 08:04.870
And they just trained you on it and you're like, okay, here's what I'm supposed to do.

08:04.870 --> 08:05.530
Right, exactly.

08:05.530 --> 08:08.110
So I've tried to follow that while also being, you know, quiet about it.

08:08.710 --> 08:11.830
Um, take him in and he's like, okay, so, so show me what you found.

08:11.830 --> 08:23.830
I pull up that slide and, uh, you know, the first, the first slide, you just, because it's so generic, it's no reaction, but then going to like the, maybe the second slide or, or even the third slide, he's just like, okay, stop.

08:23.830 --> 08:26.510
Like, stop, did you read this?

08:27.770 --> 08:37.600
And I don't answer, but I just look him in the eye and I look at the screen and I'm like, of course, this, that's how you know it exists.

08:37.600 --> 08:38.920
And he definitely picked up on that.

08:38.920 --> 08:41.920
And he, uh, the conversation ended with him saying, uh, delete it.

08:42.400 --> 08:43.200
And he left the room.

08:43.200 --> 08:43.300
Yeah.

08:43.300 --> 08:44.500
And we never spoke of it again.

08:44.500 --> 08:47.680
He's cutting you some slack there in essence, without me knowing.

08:47.680 --> 08:48.000
Yes.

08:48.000 --> 08:48.300
Yeah.

08:48.300 --> 08:49.300
You didn't read it.

08:49.680 --> 08:52.060
Uh, so you're not in any trouble that's here.

08:52.060 --> 08:52.600
Delete it.

08:52.840 --> 09:03.030
And also, as I came to learn, um, you know, it, certain material, uh, you get exposed to, and it's, you're kind of marked for life that that happened.

09:03.030 --> 09:06.270
And, uh, it's probably not good for your career at a minimum.

09:06.390 --> 09:09.990
We've seen other whistleblower friends of ours have, uh, experiences like that.

09:09.990 --> 09:10.650
They're marked.

09:10.810 --> 09:11.110
Yeah.

09:11.410 --> 09:11.590
Yeah.

09:12.030 --> 09:13.110
Didn't realize that at the time.

09:13.110 --> 09:20.870
Um, so that happened, uh, I sit on that for a few days, didn't sit right with me cause I'm still thinking like, well, that's not what we're supposed to do.

09:20.870 --> 09:26.990
I could do that, but everything, supposedly everything we do on those systems, every click, every keystroke is monitored.

09:26.990 --> 09:30.410
So like, I just, I need to self-preservation.

09:30.730 --> 09:33.110
I need to do the, keep doing the right thing here.

09:33.450 --> 09:35.730
So I go to his boss or his boss's boss.

09:36.410 --> 09:38.230
I, I changed my approach.

09:38.230 --> 09:39.190
I don't say what it is.

09:39.190 --> 09:40.230
I don't show it to them.

09:40.870 --> 09:41.950
Um, I don't print it out.

09:41.950 --> 09:47.070
And I just say, uh, ma'am, uh, we have a, a spillage incident.

09:47.070 --> 09:48.450
I believe it's SAP material.

09:48.950 --> 09:52.610
Um, could you please provide guidance on, on how to handle this?

09:52.990 --> 10:07.710
And so, uh, through that, uh, I was connected to, uh, our parent offices, uh, special access, special access program control officer, um, had a meeting set up to go meet with them a few days later that happened.

10:09.420 --> 10:13.100
I go to that meeting, uh, uh, in a.

10:13.100 --> 10:16.800
SAP F, uh, so where this material is supposed to be stored and handled.

10:17.340 --> 10:19.520
And this person says, okay, show me the material.

10:19.640 --> 10:21.640
So, uh, I sit down.

10:22.220 --> 10:22.860
Round two.

10:22.860 --> 10:23.220
Right.

10:23.220 --> 10:23.640
Exactly.

10:23.640 --> 10:24.520
Well, you're showing the material.

10:25.060 --> 10:26.940
I sit down, I pull it up.

10:27.060 --> 10:30.440
It's like, it's right there at the top of the shared servers though.

10:30.440 --> 10:32.060
I'm not like it's, it's almost instant.

10:32.060 --> 10:32.800
Like it's right there.

10:33.800 --> 10:34.600
Uh, I pull it up.

10:34.600 --> 10:36.140
I start scrolling through it from the bottom.

10:36.140 --> 10:37.100
I get no reaction.

10:37.100 --> 10:38.260
Then he says, okay, let me look at it.

10:38.300 --> 10:39.260
He takes my chair.

10:39.680 --> 10:41.480
He goes through, he scrolls through it.

10:41.860 --> 10:42.940
No reaction on his face.

10:42.940 --> 10:43.060
I'm.

10:43.100 --> 10:44.760
Watching him very closely at this point.

10:44.760 --> 10:47.480
Cause I'm exceptionally curious about all of this.

10:47.980 --> 10:48.860
No reaction.

10:49.630 --> 10:55.290
Uh, then he scrolls through it again and he makes a very deliberate, uh, scene

10:55.330 --> 11:01.360
where he pauses on Lou Elizondo's slide and starts guffawing in a very, uh,

11:02.010 --> 11:07.430
non-believable way and saying, somebody's having a joke, uh, this, uh, you

11:07.430 --> 11:08.890
don't need to worry about this.

11:09.050 --> 11:09.590
You can go.

11:10.440 --> 11:13.320
And that's not the reaction I was expecting, I was expecting to at the

11:13.320 --> 11:14.700
very least sign the paper.

11:14.700 --> 11:15.020
Right.

11:15.020 --> 11:20.900
Saying, you know, this incident happened, reported it, signed it, you know, it's done.

11:21.690 --> 11:25.220
Uh, so, you know, I, I try to ask him, like, are you, are you sure?

11:25.220 --> 11:26.420
Like, do I need to sign anything?

11:26.420 --> 11:27.420
He's like, nope, you can go.

11:27.500 --> 11:35.880
And so I left that room and, uh, never, ever had anything about that incident come up again.

11:36.180 --> 11:39.540
Except immediately you went and checked again for the file.

11:39.680 --> 11:39.880
Yeah.

11:39.880 --> 11:42.540
